<title>ITALY: Italy's Ifil H1 96 pretax profit falls.</title>
<headline>Italy's Ifil H1 96 pretax profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons pretax profit		   349    vs   374</p>
<p>    Parent pretax profit		 151    vs   114</p>
<p>Note - Ifil is an Agnelli family holding company which groups together different interests.  </p>
<p>    Cons net financial position	164    vs   (26)</p>
<p>    Cons net equity		    3,580    vs 3,434</p>
<p>Note - Ifil said its net financial position at the end of September, taking account of the acquisition of a further one percent share in Fiat from Alcatel Alsthom for 175 billion, was positive for around 20 billion lire.</p>
<p>The board had decided to propose at the next shareholders' meeting to set aside 100 billion to buy back Ifil shares.</p>
<p>The group said it expected full year results for 1996 to be better than those for 1995.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
